I have found a work around on my side implementing a custom hostname verifier (see Kotlin code below) and using that instead of the CXF DefaultHostnameVerifier. That said, I (and maybe others) would still appreciate a fix in HttpCore NIO to work with default CXF configuration.

 
{code:java}
class CustomHostnameVerifier private constructor() : HostnameVerifier {

    companion object {
        val INSTANCE = CustomHostnameVerifier()
    }

