Just wondering does my following understand correctly? High level wise, the generic model has 3 parts:

1) Generic Authorization static data, which includes authorizables, privileges, and corresponding backend metadata: so new engine will need to extend implementation to cover these pieces, e.g. Define authorization model, Define privilege model with authorization model and action factory;

2) A generic Authorization processing engine, which includes action factory and authorization methods: new engine will need to extend implementation to cover these pieces, e.g. Define action factory and imply methods;

3) A policy enforcement plugin running on apache components side: hook and binding: e.g. Implement one hook and binding.

